@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# M3 plan: detail screen (grid, tag line, speed bar, notes, Older details)
+
+Spec: `docs/specs/2026-10-16-simplification-design.md` §2.4 (detail), §3.2 (grid), §4 step 4 (`getSpotLegacy` on mount),
+D26 (archive). Features: M3-01 this plan + `formatLegacyDetails` · M3-02 detail rewrite · M3-03 walkthrough ·
+M3-04 review. Each task: RED test first, then code; `check.sh` green per commit.
+
+Starting point (after M2): `app/spot/[id]/index.tsx` = 240 pt hero `Image` (`spot-photo-0`) + horizontal 88 pt strip
+(`spot-photo-1..`) + title + "Notes" label/paragraph. No tags, no speed, no legacy. Header "Edit" → edit route.
+`PhotoGrid`, `SpeedScale readonly`, `ChipGroup` exist (M2). `getSpotLegacy(db, id)` exists, never called; it
+`JSON.parse`s without a catch, so bad JSON **rejects**.
+
+## Layout (M3-02), §2.4 order, no `Section` boxes, no headers but "Notes"
+
+| # | Element | Shown when | Built from |
+|--:|---------|------------|------------|
+| 1 | Photo grid | ≥ 1 photo | `PhotoGrid photos={spotPhotos(spot, media)}` (primary first). No `onPressPhoto` in M3 (tiles role `image`); M4 adds `onPressPhoto={(i) => router.push(/spot/<id>/photos?index=i)}`. |
+| 1′ | "Add photos" tile | 0 photos | `PhotoGrid photos={[]} trailing={<AddPhotosTile/>}` (grid renders only the trailing square). Tile: `Pressable accessibilityRole="button" accessibilityLabel="Add photos"`, '+' icon; `onPress → router.push('/spot/<id>/edit')`. |
+| 2 | Title | always | `getSpotDisplayName(spot)` (D4 label when unnamed). No Draft badge (D20). |
+| 3 | Tag line | `feature_types.length > 0 \|\| stopped` | `ChipGroup` of read-only `Tag`s: one per `feature_types` entry in stored order (`FEATURE_TYPE_LABELS`), then "Skate stopped" when `stopped === true` (absent when false). |
+| 4 | Natural speed | `natural_speed !== undefined` (never `!`; 0 = None) | `<SpeedScale readonly value={spot.natural_speed} />` (label 'Natural speed: <word>'). |
+| 5 | Notes | `spot.notes` non-empty | small "Notes" label + paragraph (as today; same label as edit). |
+| 6 | Older details | `rows.length > 0` | disclosure, below. |
+
+Read-only `Tag` (new, in `src/components/Chip.tsx`, exported): `View` + `Text`, **no** `accessibilityRole`, no
+`Pressable`, so VoiceOver reads it as text, not a checkbox (M3-04). Same shape as `Chip`. Prop `tone?: 'default' |
+'stopped'`; `stopped` → `borderColor: palette.red[500]`, text `palette.red[700]`, background white (outline only).
+Spot with only location + photos → grid + title, nothing else (spec: "a complete spot").
+
+## Older details (M3-02)
+
+- State in the screen: `legacy: SpotLegacy | null` (initial `null`), `open = false`.
+- `const db = useSQLiteContext()`. `useEffect(() => { let live = true; getSpotLegacy(db, id).then((l) => live &&
+  setLegacy(l)).catch((e) => console.warn('Older details unreadable', id, e)); return () => { live = false }; },
+  [db, id])` → **called once per mount**, not on store updates (deps are `db`, `id` only; spot/media are not deps).
+  Bad JSON → one `console.warn` (not `error`: the suite must stay at zero `console.error`), `legacy` stays `null`,
+  no disclosure, no crash.
+- `rows = legacy ? formatLegacyDetails(legacy, units) : []`, `units` from `useSettingsStore((s) => s.units)`
+  (switching units on Profile re-renders the rows without a re-fetch). `rows.length === 0` (null or all-empty
+  archive) → nothing rendered, not even the header.
+- Header: `Pressable accessibilityRole="button" accessibilityState={{ expanded: open }}`, text "Older details" +
+  chevron (`chevron-forward` / `chevron-down`), small gray. **Collapsed by default**; tap toggles. Open → one row
+  per entry: label (gray) left, value right, wraps. Read-only; edit/save never touch `legacy_json` (`updateSpot`
+  has no such field).
+
+## `formatLegacyDetails` (M3-01, done) — `src/utils/legacy-details.ts`
+
+`formatLegacyDetails(legacy: Record<string, unknown>, units: UnitSystem): { label: string; value: string }[]`.
+`SpotLegacy` became a `type` alias (was `interface`) so `getSpotLegacy`'s result passes without a cast.
+Rows in this table's order, then unknown keys (stored order, key humanised: `old_field_x` → 'Old field x'), then the
+`raw_*` columns. Skipped: `undefined`, `null`, blank strings, empty arrays. A value of an unexpected type falls back
+to plain text (string as is, number `String`, boolean Yes/No, object `JSON.stringify`); never throws.
+
+| Key | Label | Value |
+|-----|-------|-------|
+| `custom_type` | Custom type | as stored ('curved rail') |
+| `shape` | Shape | as stored (free text: 'kinked', 'DFD') |
+| `length_m` | Length | `displayLength(m, units)`: '12.0 ft' / '3.7 m' |
+| `height_m` | Height | same |
+| `width_m` | Width | same |
+| `material` | Material | `_` → space ('steel', 'painted steel') |
+| `stop_type` | Stop type | `_` → space ('knobs') |
+| `stop_description` | Stop description | as stored |
+| `removable` | Removable | Yes / No |
+| `difficulty` | Difficulty | 'n/5' |
+| `landing_difficulty` | Landing difficulty | 'n/5' |
+| `landing_surface` | Landing surface | `_` → space ('snow built') |
+| `intensity` | Intensity | 'n/5' |
+| `bustability` | Bustability | 'n/5' |
+| `bustability_notes` | Bustability notes | as stored |
+| `setup_options` | Setup options | '2 options: winch; drop in platform + 2 speed humps' (items `+`, options `;`, quantity > 1 prefixed; unreadable option → its JSON) |
+| `raw_feature` / `raw_in_run` / `raw_landing` / `raw_metadata` | Feature / In-run / Landing / Other (unreadable) | verbatim |
+
+Tests `src/__tests__/legacy-details.test.ts` (9): feature sample Imperial (6 rows, exact order) · Metric '3.7 m' ·
+humanised key (`stop_description`, `old_field_x`) · `{}` → `[]` · full M1 fixture (`v2-spots.json` `fullLegacy`, 16
+rows) · unknown keys after known, raw last · empties skipped, odd types plain · unreadable setup option · a typed
+`SpotLegacy` accepted.
+
+## M3-02 tests (`src/__tests__/spot-detail.test.tsx`, RED first)
+
+Mock: `jest.mock('@/src/db', () => ({ ...jest.requireActual('@/src/db'), getSpotLegacy: jest.fn() }))`, default
+`mockResolvedValue(null)` in `beforeEach`. Every render awaits the effect (`await waitFor(() =>
+expect(getSpotLegacy).toHaveBeenCalled())`, then `findBy…`/`act`) so no act() warning reaches `console.error`.
+`spot-photos.test.tsx` also renders the detail screen: same mock there, and its `spot-photo-N` ids become
+`photo-tile-N`.
+
+1. rail+ledge, stopped, speed 3, notes 'low' → Tags 'Rail', 'Ledge', 'Skate stopped' (flattened `borderColor ===
+   palette.red[500]`), label 'Natural speed: Enough', text 'low'.
+2. `stopped: false` → no 'Skate stopped'; `natural_speed` undefined → no label starting 'Natural speed';
+   `natural_speed: 0` → 'Natural speed: None' (0 is real).
+3. 'Skate stopped' and the type tags have no `checkbox`/`button` role (`queryAllByRole('checkbox')` empty).
+4. 5 media → `photo-tile-0..4`, primary first; 0 media → 'Add photos' button, press → `router.push('/spot/<id>/edit')`.
+5. legacy `{ material: 'steel' }` → 'Older details' shown, no 'Material' until pressed, then 'Material' + 'steel';
+   `null` → no 'Older details'; `{}` → none; `getSpotLegacy` called once with `(db, id)`, still once after a store
+   update + rerender (M3-04); rejected promise → no disclosure, `console.warn` once, no throw (M3-04).
+6. Units: legacy `{ length_m: 3.6576 }` open → '12.0 ft'; `setUnits(Metric)` → '3.7 m'.
+7. Tree has no 'Feature', 'In-Run', 'Landing', 'Details', 'Draft', 'Type' texts; minimal spot (name + 1 photo) texts
+   are exactly the title.
+8. Header: render `options.headerRight()` off the mocked `Stack.Screen` (pattern in `spots-sort-search.test.tsx`
+   l.172), press 'Edit' → `router.push('/spot/<id>/edit')`. **No such test exists today** (M3-02 step 4 says
+   "existing test kept"); M3-02 adds it.
+
+## Order of commits
+
+M3-01: RED `fb8e20e`, GREEN `1a327ac`, this plan. M3-02: RED tests 1–8 → `Tag` → screen rewrite → spot-photos test ids
+→ GREEN. M3-03: scratch renders → walkthrough doc. M3-04: diff to `reviews/m3.diff`, Opus review, fixes, `refactor:`.
+
+## Unresolved questions
+
+Builder's calls (spec §10), for Michael in the progress entry:
+- Enum values shown lower case as stored ('steel', 'snow built'), not 'Steel': the feature's test fixes 'steel'.
+- Small widths in Imperial read '0.2 ft' (not inches); `displayLength` as is.
+- Keep the small "Notes" label on detail (edit has one); the spec only says "Notes, only when present".
+- M3 tiles don't open anything until the M4 viewer lands.
